      "text": "Participating Faculty Members The participating faculty are drawn from the Departments of Chemistry and Biochemistry , Physics , Biomedical Sciences , and reflect a wide diversity of research interests and expertise. Brief descriptions of the research areas represented by individual faculty members are summarized below. Chemistry and Biochemistry Name/Contact Info Research Topics Rommie Amaro Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Amaro Research Group ramaro@ucsd.edu Computational Chemistry and Biophysics Itay Budin Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Budin Research Group ibudin@ucsd.edu Biochemistry and synthetic biology of cell membranes Geoffrey Chang Professor of Pharmacy g1chang@ucsd.edu Structural biology of transporters Kevin Corbett Professor, Cell and Molecular Medicine; Head of Laboratory of Structural Biology at the Ludwig Institute for Cancer Research Structural Biology Lab kcorbett@ucsd.edu We use biochemical and macromolecular structure tools to understand the organization of meiotic chromosomes, the regulation of meiotic DNA recombination to create crossovers, and the checkpoint mechanisms that monitor these events. Galia Debelouchina Associate Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Debelouchina Lab gdebelouchina@ucsd.edu Chemical and spectroscopic approaches for structural biology of complex biological systems Lalit Deshmukh Associate Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Deshmukh Research Group ldeshmukh@ucsd.edu Solution NMR spectroscopy, retroviruses, protein and nucleic acid biochemistry Neal Devaraj Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Devaraj Research Group ndevaraj@ucsd.edu Tetrazine Cycloadditions for bioorthogonal chemistry and functional materials. Imaging and in vivo chemistry Fleur Ferguson Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Ferguson Lab flferguson@ucsd.edu Targeted protein degradation, oncology, neurodegeneration Michael Gilson Professor, Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Science; Chair in Computer-Aided Drug Design, Co-Director UCSD Center for Drug Discovery Innovation Gilson Lab mgilson@ucsd.edu Computer-aided molecular design, physical chemistry of molecular recognition, drug discovery, host-guest chemistry, cheminformatics, simulations and molecular modeling. Alex Guseman Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry aguseman@ucsd.edu Biophysical basis of protein glycan recognition Mark Herzik Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Herzik Research Group mherzik@ucsd.edu Elucidating the mechanisms of macromolecular transport into and within mitochondria Adrian Jinich Assistant Professor of Pharmacy and Chemistry and Biochemistry ajinich@ucsd.edu AI for understanding orphan enzyme families Lisa Jones Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry lijones@ucsd.edu Structural Proteomics using mass spectrometry Simpson Joseph Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry Joseph Lab sjoseph@ucsd.edu Biochemistry & Biophysics: ribosome structure, function and dynamics; discovery of novel antibiotics Elizabeth A. Komives Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Komives Lab ekomives@ucsd.edu Structure, function, dynamics and thermodynamics of protein-protein interactions: NMR, mass spectrometry and kinetics Alexis Komor Associate Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Komor Lab akomor@ucsd.edu DNA damage and repair; Genome editing; Chemical biology of aging April Lukowski Assistant Professor of Pharmacy and Oceanography alukowski@ucsd.edu Novel marine-derived biosynthetic enzymes; discovery, enzymology, and generation of new natural Colleen McHugh Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The McHugh Research Group c1mchugh@ucsd.edu RNA-protein interactions; Assembly of RNPs; Structural biology of multimeric complexes Tatiana Mishanina Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Mishanina Lab tmishanina@UCSD.EDU Molecular mechanisms of transcription in bacteria and human mitochondria Johannes Schoeneberg Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Schoeneberg Lab jschoeneberg@ucsd.edu Cellular organelle dynamics by lattice light sheet microscopy Douglas Smith Associate Professor of Physics des0free@gmail.com Mechanical manipulation and imaging of single DNA molecules; Viral DNA packaging in bacteriophages phi29, lambda, and T4; Function of ATP-dependent molecular motors; Single polymer dynamics (polymer physics, DNA properties, rheology); Chromatin assembly and structure; Enzyme mediated DNA looping; Restriction endonuclease function; Physics of knot formation Roger Sunahara Professor of Pharmacology rsunahara@ucsd.edu Mechanism of cell signaling in the G protein-coupled receptor (GPCR) field. Susan Taylor Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry Professor of Pharmacology Howard Hughes Medical Institute Susan S. Taylor Lab staylor@ucsd.edu Structure, Function, Dynamics, and Localization of PKA as a Prototype for the Protein Kinase Superfamily. Navtej Toor Assoc. Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry ntoor@ucsd.edu Structure and Function of Introns and Retroelements Elizabeth Villa Professor of Molecular Biology Villa Lab evilla@ucsd.edu Structural Cell Biology, Cryo-Electron Microscopy, Multiscale modeling Dong Wang Professor Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences Wang Lab dongwang@ucsd.edu Molecular Mechanisms of DNA Damage Processing Pathways Wei Wang Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry Wei Wang Research Group wew002@ucsd.edu Inference of gene regulatory networks and determination of protein specificity Jin Zhang Professor of Pharmacology jiz175@ucsd.edu Spatiotemporal regulation of signal transduction Brian Zid Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry The Zid Research Group zid@ucsd.edu Dynamics of mRNA localization in the control of gene expression.",
